From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Nepomuceno Marcos <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 13:35:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] comms: branding + one-icon model (applicationId, no LAUNCHER,
 OPEN action)

Cloud-Comms mail fork, patch 1 of the series (see ea_cloud-comms/forks/README.md):
- applicationId eu.faircode.email -> com.diegonmarcos.comms.mail (namespace and
  resources untouched; ${applicationId}/${namespace} placeholders follow).
- ActivityMain loses the LAUNCHER category (one-icon model: the Cloud-Comms hub
  is the only home-screen icon) and gains the constellation OPEN intent-filter
  (com.diegonmarcos.comms.action.OPEN) the hub/SuperApp use to launch it.
TODO follow-up patches: provisioning (imap/smtps SNI :443 defaults), exporter
(contract tables + signature gate on OPEN), constellation top bar.
---
 app/build.gradle                 |  7 ++++++-
 app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/build.gradle b/app/build.gradle
index 40836d226d..333b943c6d 100644
--- a/app/build.gradle
+++ b/app/build.gradle
@@ -24,7 +24,12 @@ android {
     // https://apilevels.com/
     // https://developer.android.com/studio/releases#api-level-support
     defaultConfig {
-        applicationId "eu.faircode.email"
+        // Cloud-Comms fork: own applicationId so the fork installs alongside any
+        // stock FairEmail and joins the constellation (the hub opens it via the
+        // com.diegonmarcos.comms.action.OPEN intent). namespace stays
+        // eu.faircode.email — resources/R untouched; the ${applicationId} and
+        // ${namespace} manifest placeholders follow this id automatically.
+        applicationId "com.diegonmarcos.comms.mail"
         compileSdk = 37
         minSdkVersion 23
         targetSdkVersion 37
diff --git a/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml b/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
index d2139a6aa6..897829a3ab 100644
--- a/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -171,14 +171,27 @@
                 android:name="android.app.shortcuts"
                 android:resource="@xml/shortcuts" />
 
+            <!-- Cloud-Comms fork (one-icon model): NO LAUNCHER category — the
+                 Cloud-Comms hub is the only home-screen icon; it opens this app
+                 via the constellation OPEN action below (contract::launch_action).
+                 MAIN/APP_EMAIL kept so the system still resolves it as the
+                 device's email app where applicable. -->
             <intent-filter>
                 <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
 
                 <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
-                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
                 <category android:name="android.intent.category.APP_EMAIL" />
             </intent-filter>
 
+            <!-- Constellation open action — how the hub / Cloud-SuperApp launch
+                 this icon-less fork: Intent("com.diegonmarcos.comms.action.OPEN")
+                 .setPackage(applicationId). Optional THREAD_ID extra deep-links
+                 a conversation (wired with the exporter patch). -->
+            <intent-filter>
+                <action android:name="com.diegonmarcos.comms.action.OPEN" />
+                <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
+            </intent-filter>
+
             <intent-filter>
                 <action android:name="${applicationId}.REFRESH" />
                 <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
